    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Taylor Ward** headline our lineup as the strongest plays, both boasting efficiency scores of 66.5. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Germ\u00e1n M\u00e1rquez (xERA 5.64), with the optimization model capitalizing on a projected #2 spot in the order, which provides significant run-scoring potential. **Taylor Ward** remains a elite play despite the 45% rain risk in his contest; his score is buoyed by a substantial +16% park factor and the expected upside of leading off against a lefty. While **Gavin Sheets** sits at a strong 63.2, his start against Zac Gallen is a high-reward play driven by his platoon advantage and expected cleanup duties, offering a high ceiling despite the opponent\u2019s solid arm. \n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult choice involved **Dylan Beavers**, who fell just short of the starting rotation with a score of 44.0. While **Dylan Beavers** benefits from the same favorable park factors as **Taylor Ward**, the optimizer prioritized **Tyler Freeman** (60.18) due to the higher projected volume and the distinct advantage of facing a starter with a slow delivery, which increases the probability of a stolen base\u2014a critical requirement given our strategic emphasis on SB scarcity. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains on the IL, leaving our infield depth to be carried by the consistency of **Jonathan Aranda** and **Bryson Stott**. \n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding the rain risk for **Taylor Ward**, as any delay could dampen his output or lead to a shortened outing. Additionally, since the lineups for **Masyn Winn**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Luis Arraez** are technically still pending, we are locked into these projected positions. Should **Daulton Varsho** be moved down the order, his utility as a stolen base threat against a slow-moving pitcher remains his primary value driver, helping offset the minor penalty of his #7 spot. We are proceeding with this lineup to maximize our daily efficiency and maintain our position in the 5x5 standings.",
